# Project Structure

Shopify theme starter with portable components, modern build pipeline, and Docker-based development environment.

## Core Directories

### `/_js/` - JavaScript/TypeScript Source

Main source directory for all JavaScript/TypeScript code:

**Core Modules:**

- `/core/` - Utilities, helpers, shared modules
  - `/shopify/`, `/cart/`, `/cart-v2/` - Business logic
  - `/dom/`, `/viewport/`, `/animation/` - UI utilities
  - `/analytics/`, `/accessibility/`, `/network/` - Integrations

**Portable Components:**

- `/sections/` - Self-contained Shopify sections
  - Structure: `section.liquid`, `styles.scss`, `index.ts`
- `/snippets/` - Reusable UI components
  - Structure: `snippet.liquid`, `styles.scss`, optional `index.tsx`
- `/web-components/` - Framework-agnostic custom elements
  - Structure: `component.ts`, `index.ts`, `style.shadow.scss`, `ssr.scss`

**Other Modules:**

- `/theme/` - Global scripts (`offcanvas-menu.ts`, `lazysizes.ts`)
- `/standalone/` - Independent bundles
- `/product/`, `/cart/` - Feature-specific functionality

### `/_sass/` - SCSS Source

Global SCSS files and style guide:

- `master.scss` - Main stylesheet entry
- `inline-css.scss` - Critical inline styles
- `/core/` - Style guide modules (colors, typography, spacing, mixins)

### `/devops/` - Build & DevOps Infrastructure

- `/ci/` - GitHub Actions workflows for CI/CD
- `/codegen/` - Code generation tools (TypeScript types, CSS modules)
- `/src/` - Build system source code (Gulp tasks, webpack configs)
- `/bin/` - Compiled build utilities
- `bb.ts` - Task runner configuration (Babashka-inspired)

### Shopify Theme Structure

- `/assets/` - Compiled assets (managed by build)
- `/sections/`, `/snippets/` - Theme files + compiled portables
- `/templates/` - Page templates (JSON)
- `/layout/` - Theme layouts
- `/locales/` - Internationalization
- `/config/` - Theme settings

## Portable Components

Three types of self-contained components:

1. **Portable Sections** (`_js/sections/`)
   - Structure: `section.liquid`, `styles.scss`, `index.ts`
   - CSS modules for scoped styles
   - Auto-loaded when section is on page

2. **Portable Snippets** (`_js/snippets/`)
   - Structure: `snippet.liquid`, `styles.scss`, optional `index.tsx`
   - React/TSX support available
   - Reusable UI components

3. **Portable Web Components** (`_js/web-components/`)
   - Structure: `component.ts`, `index.ts`, `style.shadow.scss`, `ssr.scss`
   - Shadow DOM isolation
   - Framework-agnostic

## Development Commands

All tasks via `bb` command:

**Essential Tasks:**

```bash
bb ci                 # Run all CI checks (lint, test, typecheck, build, themecheck)
bb build              # Build all assets
bb deploy-dev         # Deploy to your virtual (development) theme
bb commit-assets      # Commit build assets and codegen artefacts
bb fetch              # Download theme files from Shopify
```

**Code Quality:**

```bash
bb test               # Run unit test suite
bb lint               # Lint the code
bb typecheck          # TypeScript validation
bb themecheck         # Run Shopify Theme Check
bb prettify           # Format files
bb organize-imports   # Sort imports in TS/JS files
```

## Development Workflow

### Getting Started

1. **Environment Setup:**
   - Docker container provides consistent development environment
   - All dependencies and tools pre-configured in container
   - No action needed to get started

2. **Development Commands:**
   - `bb build` - Build all assets for production
   - `bb test` - Run test suite
   - `bb lint` - Run linters with autofixes
   - `bb ci` - **CRITICAL: Run before committing** (see [project-build-validation.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/project-build-validation.mdc))

### File Organization Best Practices

**Portable Components:**

- Keep all related files (Liquid, SCSS, TS) in the same folder
- Use index files for component exports
- Follow naming conventions: `component-name/component-name.liquid`

**TypeScript Modules:**

- Follow patterns in [lang-typescript.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/lang-typescript.mdc)
- Use named exports. Avoid using barrel exports.
- Leverage TypeScript strict mode

**Styling:**

- Global styles in `_sass/` directory
- Component styles as CSS modules in portable folders
- Use style guide variables from `_sass/core/`

### Build and Deployment

1. **Local Development:**

   ```bash
   bb build           # Build assets
   bb ci              # Run full CI suite
   ```

2. **Deployment:**

   ```bash
   bb deploy-dev      # Deploy to your development theme
   ```

3. **Quality Checks:**
   - Always run `./run-task ci` before committing
   - Fix any linting errors or test failures
   - Ensure TypeScript compilation succeeds

